{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status = \"Done\"","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","change 1815"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","jql query","status category","active set","done status","workflow","client workflow","scope"],"propositions":["jql_active hardcodes status != \"Done\" and incorrectly includes Resolved/Closed/Cancelled statuses in the active working set for non-DIG/REB workflows","jql_done_recent hardcodes status = \"Done\" and misses resolved issues, failing to populate the recent-Done snapshot for workflows with custom Done-equivalent statuses","Switching Done predicate from literal status = \"Done\" to statusCategory = Done makes active/done scoping workflow-agnostic and compatible with all Jira status categories","The fix updates jql_active to use statusCategory != Done and jql_done_recent to use statusCategory = Done with ORDER BY updated DESC, preserving per-project scoping unchanged"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787764723640885001,"uuid":"26562b48-6077-406b-972a-5d5026c07412"}